{"id":7,"title":"Reliability","syllabus_module":"Module 7","question":"If each red-flag rule is a component, how reliable is the system for one user?","code":[{"label":"Rules as series and parallel components","file":"analysis/07_phishscore_reliability.R","start_line":74,"code":"# ---- Module 7: each selected rule as a component ----\nrule_rates <- data.frame(\n  rule = features,\n  d = vapply(features, function(f) mean(test[[f]][truth] == 1), numeric(1)),\n  f = vapply(features, function(f) mean(test[[f]][!truth] == 1), numeric(1))\n)\nfires <- as.matrix(test[, features]) == 1\nsystem_rates <- data.frame(\n  system = c(\"parallel (any fires)\", \"series (all fire)\"),\n  detect_predicted = c(parallel_prob(rule_rates$d), series_prob(rule_rates$d)),\n  detect_empirical = c(mean(apply(fires[truth, ], 1, any)), mean(apply(fires[truth, ], 1, all))),\n  false_alarm_predicted = c(parallel_prob(rule_rates$f), series_prob(rule_rates$f)),\n  false_alarm_empirical = c(mean(apply(fires[!truth, ], 1, any)),\n                            mean(apply(fires[!truth, ], 1, all)))\n)"},{"label":"Pairwise rule dependence (chi-square)","file":"analysis/07_phishscore_reliability.R","start_line":91,"code":"\n# Pairwise rule dependence within each class (chi-square, phi).\nrule_dependence <- function(rows, label) {\n  pairs <- utils::combn(features, 2)\n  do.call(rbind, lapply(seq_len(ncol(pairs)), function(k) {\n    a <- test[[pairs[1, k]]][rows]\n    b <- test[[pairs[2, k]]][rows]\n    tab <- table(factor(a, 0:1), factor(b, 0:1))\n    ct <- suppressWarnings(stats::chisq.test(tab, correct = FALSE))\n    phi <- if (stats::sd(a) > 0 && stats::sd(b) > 0) stats::cor(a, b) else NA_real_\n    data.frame(class = label, rule_a = pairs[1, k], rule_b = pairs[2, k],\n               chi2 = unname(ct$statistic), p_value = ct$p.value, phi = phi)\n  }))\n}\ndependence <- rbind(rule_dependence(truth, \"phishing\"), rule_dependence(!truth, \"legitimate\"))\ndependence$p_holm <- stats::p.adjust(dependence$p_value, method = \"holm\")"},{"label":"User-level reliability and MTTF","file":"analysis/07_phishscore_reliability.R","start_line":110,"code":"# User level: pi = 1%, miss rate m = 1 - sensitivity, hazard h = pi * m.\npi_phish <- 0.01\nmiss <- 1 - m_main[\"sensitivity\", \"estimate\"]\nhazard <- pi_phish * miss\nn_seq <- 0:1000\nuser_curve <- data.frame(n = n_seq, reliability = user_reliability(n_seq, hazard))\nuser_plot <- ggplot(user_curve, aes(x = .data$n, y = .data$reliability)) +\n  geom_line(colour = \"#3b6fb6\", linewidth = 0.8) +\n  labs(x = \"emails received\", y = \"R(n) = P(no missed phish)\",\n       title = sprintf(\"User reliability, pi = 1%%, miss rate %.3f\", miss)) +\n  theme_minimal()\nggsave(\"outputs/figures/m7_user_reliability.png\", user_plot, width = 6, height = 4, dpi = 120)\nuser_level <- c(pi = pi_phish, miss_rate = miss, hazard = hazard,\n                r_100 = user_reliability(100, hazard), r_1000 = user_reliability(1000, hazard),\n                mttf_emails = mttf_emails(hazard), mttf_days = mttf_emails(hazard) / 50)"},{"label":"Series and parallel systems","file":"R/reliability.R","start_line":4,"code":"# Parallel system (any component fires): 1 - prod(1 - p), assuming independence.\nparallel_prob <- function(p) 1 - prod(1 - p)\n\n# Series system (all components fire): prod(p), assuming independence.\nseries_prob <- function(p) prod(p)"}],"console":["The tzdb package is not installed. Timezones will not be available to Arrow compute functions. If you get errors when using Arrow on datetimes, try running `install.packages('tzdb')` and trying again.","Selected features: has_credential, generic_greeting, has_money, subject_caps, has_urgency, at_in_url ","Train prior 0.1098; test n = 13228 (phishing 1452)","","Confusion matrix (test, threshold 0.5):","            actual","predicted    phishing legitimate","  phishing       1083        365","  legitimate      369      11411","","Metrics with Wilson 95% CI:","            estimate  lower  upper","sensitivity   0.7459 0.7228 0.7676","specificity   0.9690 0.9657 0.9720","precision     0.7479 0.7249 0.7696","f1            0.7469 0.7308 0.7624","AUC 0.9198","Precision at 1% prevalence: deployed model 0.1955; re-scored with 1% prior 0.4921","","Cross-corpus on Nigerian Fraud vs test legitimate:","                            model sensitivity specificity    auc","            in-corpus (all train)      0.8865      0.9690 0.9675"," cross-corpus (no Nigerian Fraud)      0.4732      0.9905 0.9136","Sensitivity drop: 0.4134","","Rule components (test):","             rule      d       f","   has_credential 0.7238 0.08662"," generic_greeting 0.3175 0.00127","        has_money 0.5640 0.04093","     subject_caps 0.2424 0.01087","      has_urgency 0.4793 0.08628","        at_in_url 0.0062 0.00883","               system detect_predicted detect_empirical false_alarm_predicted"," parallel (any fires)        9.678e-01           0.9036             2.163e-01","    series (all fire)        9.336e-05           0.0000             3.740e-11"," false_alarm_empirical","                0.1955","                0.0000","Rule pairs dependent (Holm p < 0.05): 16 of 30; mean phi phishing 0.070, legit 0.043","","User level: pi 0.01 miss_rate 0.2541 hazard 0.002541 r_100 0.7753 r_1000 0.07851 mttf_emails 393.5 mttf_days 7.87 ","Availability: mtbf_days 90 mttr_days 2 availability 0.9783 "," Assumption-based: lexicon and likelihoods refreshed every 90 days, 2 days degraded per refresh; drift size taken from the cross-corpus sensitivity drop of 0.413. "],"tests":[{"name":"has_credential x has_money within legitimate","h0":"rules fire independently","h1":"rules are dependent","statistic":314.52,"critical":"3.841","p_value":"6.79e-69","decision":"reject H0","effect_label":"phi","effect_value":0.1634},{"name":"subject_caps x has_urgency within legitimate","h0":"rules fire independently","h1":"rules are dependent","statistic":129.53,"critical":"3.841","p_value":"1.50e-28","decision":"reject H